                "rationale": "A credential typed directly into source is leaked the moment it is committed, and stays leaked in history even after the line is deleted. This rule looks for two independent signals: a value shaped like a real vendor credential, and a suspiciously-named binding holding a non-placeholder string.",
                "severity": "error",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a definition whose name or literal value is shaped like an embedded credential"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A form with many bindings or clauses is doing many things in one place. Splitting it — into smaller lets, a dispatch table, or separate functions per clause — usually makes each piece independently readable and testable, at the cost of naming the pieces."
              },
              "id": "giant-conditional-form",
              "properties": {
